2. `OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint` orders by `-datetime` (`DateTimeField`), but `OptimizedCursorPaginator` implements `Paginator`'s numeric `get_item_key` (`math.floor(value)` / `math.ceil(value)`) and `value_from_cursor` instead of `DateTimePaginator`'s timestamp conversion, which raises `TypeError: must be real number, not datetime.datetime` when serializing cursors."}, {"file": "src/sentry/api/paginator.py", "line": 182, "severity": "high", "category": "bug", "title": "Allowing negative cursor offsets in QuerySet slicing raises `ValueError`", "body": "Both `BasePaginator.get_result` (when `cursor.is_prev` is true and `cursor.offset < 0`) and `OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_result` (lines 877-886) pass a negative `start_offset` directly into `queryset[start_offset:stop]`. Django `QuerySet` slicing does not support negative indices and immediately raises `ValueError: Negative indexing is not supported.`, resulting in an unhandled 500 error whenever a client supplies a cursor string with a negative offset (e.g. `cursor=0:-5:1`)."}]}
